  "approach": "To reach step k, the final move comes from k - 1 or k - 2, so ways(k) = ways(k - 1) + ways(k - 2) — the Fibonacci recurrence. Starting with one way to stand at step 0 and one way to reach step 1, iterate up to n while retaining only the last two counts. The loop takes O(n) time and uses O(1) auxiliary space.",
