  "approach": "Keep the stream split into two balanced halves backed by heaps: a max-heap holds the smaller half and a min-heap holds the larger half. On each insertion, push into the max-heap, move its top into the min-heap, then rebalance so the max-heap is equal in size to or one larger than the min-heap. This guarantees the roots straddle the median. When the total count is odd the median is the max-heap root; when even it is the average of the two roots. Each insertion runs a constant number of O(log n) heap operations, and findMedian reads one or two roots in O(1).",
