  "solution": {
   "javascript": "var findWords = function(board, words) {\n    if (!board || !board.length || !board[0].length) return [];\n    const TERMINAL = '$';\n    const trie = {};\n    for (const word of words) {\n        let node = trie;\n        for (const ch of word) {\n            if (!node[ch]) node[ch] = {};\n            node = node[ch];\n        }\n        node[TERMINAL] = word;\n    }\n    const rows = board.length, cols = board[0].length;\n    const found = [];\n    const dirs = [[1, 0], [-1, 0], [0, 1], [0, -1]];\n    const search = (row, col, parent) => {\n        const ch = board[row][col];\n        const node = parent[ch];\n        if (node === undefined) return;\n        if (Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(node, TERMINAL)) {\n            found.push(node[TERMINAL]);\n            delete node[TERMINAL];\n        }\n        board[row][col] = '#';\n        for (const [dr, dc] of dirs) {\n            const nr = row + dr, nc = col + dc;\n            if (nr >= 0 && nr < rows && nc >= 0 && nc < cols && board[nr][nc] !== '#') {\n                search(nr, nc, node);\n            }\n        }\n        board[row][col] = ch;\n        if (Object.keys(node).length === 0) delete parent[ch];\n    };\n    for (let row = 0; row < rows; row++) {\n        for (let col = 0; col < cols; col++) {\n            search(row, col, trie);\n        }\n    }\n    return found;\n};",
   "python": "from typing import List\n\n\nclass Solution:\n    def findWords(self, board: List[List[str]], words: List[str]) -> List[str]:\n        if not board or not board[0]:\n            return []\n\n        terminal = '$'\n        trie = {}\n        for word in words:\n            node = trie\n            for ch in word:\n                node = node.setdefault(ch, {})\n            node[terminal] = word\n\n        rows, cols = len(board), len(board[0])\n        found = []\n\n        def search(row: int, col: int, parent: dict) -> None:\n            ch = board[row][col]\n            node = parent.get(ch)\n            if node is None:\n                return\n\n            word = node.pop(terminal, None)\n            if word is not None:\n                found.append(word)\n\n            board[row][col] = '#'\n            for dr, dc in ((1, 0), (-1, 0), (0, 1), (0, -1)):\n                nr, nc = row + dr, col + dc\n                if 0 <= nr < rows and 0 <= nc < cols and board[nr][nc] != '#':\n                    search(nr, nc, node)\n            board[row][col] = ch\n\n            if not node:\n                parent.pop(ch, None)\n\n        for row in range(rows):\n            for col in range(cols):\n                search(row, col, trie)\n\n        return found\n"
  },
  "approach": "Insert every dictionary word into a trie so a single board path can represent a shared prefix of many words at once, and exploration stops immediately when no word continues the current prefix. Run DFS from each cell, descending the matching trie branch; temporarily mark a visited cell with '#' so it is not reused within one word, then restore it on backtrack. When a trie node holds a terminal word, record it and remove the terminal marker to avoid duplicate answers; pruning empty branches speeds later searches. With S the total dictionary character count, R*C the board size, and L the longest word, worst-case time is O(S + R*C*3^L). Auxiliary space is O(S + L) for the trie and recursion, excluding the returned words.",
